    {prompt:"Have you ever faced a problem while working on a project? What was the issue, and how did you solve it? Please describe the situation in detail.",promptKo:"프로젝트를 수행하면서 문제를 겪은 적이 있나요? 문제는 무엇이었고 어떻게 해결했나요? 자세히 설명해 주세요.",text:"Yes, I once faced a pretty serious problem when I was working on the finance team at my previous company. At the time, I was responsible for managing the company's cash reserves. We were managing about 140 billion won, and our main goal was to manage those funds safely while generating additional returns. So, we invested a significant portion of the money in fixed-income securities. Unfortunately, an unexpected political situation created a lot of uncertainty in the financial markets, and bond yields suddenly rose sharply. As a result, the market value of our bond investments dropped significantly, and we suffered a substantial investment loss. To make matters worse, the company's operating performance was already weak at the time, so the investment loss put even more pressure on the company's financial performance. Naturally, senior management was extremely concerned about the situation, and they put tremendous pressure on our team to recover the losses. The situation became so stressful that two members of our team eventually left the company. That left the rest of us struggling to deal with the situation with fewer people. At that point, I realized that we couldn't simply wait for the market to recover. We needed to completely reassess our investment strategy and come up with a way to minimize further losses.",ko:"이전 회사 재무팀에서 회사의 현금 보유액을 운용할 때 심각한 문제를 겪었습니다. 당시 약 1,400억 원을 운용했고, 안전하게 자금을 관리하면서 추가 수익을 창출하는 것이 목표였습니다. 상당 부분을 채권형 증권에 투자했는데 예상치 못한 정치 상황으로 금융시장의 불확실성이 커지고 채권 금리가 급등했습니다. 그 결과 채권 투자자산의 시장가치가 크게 떨어져 상당한 투자손실이 발생했습니다. 당시 회사의 영업 실적도 좋지 않아 상황은 더 악화됐고 경영진은 손실 만회를 강하게 요구했습니다. 압박으로 팀원 두 명이 회사를 떠나 남은 인원이 더 적은 사람으로 상황을 처리해야 했습니다. 그때 시장 회복만 기다릴 수 없다고 판단했고 투자전략을 전면 재검토해 추가 손실을 최소화할 방법을 찾아야 했습니다."}
