    {prompt:"Describe a library you often visit. Where is it located? What does it look like from the outside? How is the interior arranged? Provide as many details as possible.",promptKo:"자주 가는 도서관을 묘사해 주세요. 어디에 있고 외관은 어떠하며 내부는 어떻게 구성되어 있나요?",text:"The library I used to visit most often is called Negeok Library. When I lived alone, it was located very close to my place. It was only about a five-minute walk away, so whenever I didn't have any plans, I would often go there by myself and spend a few hours reading. From the outside, [it looks like a fairly modern building / it's not particularly large, but it looks clean and well maintained]. As soon as you walk in, there's an information desk near the entrance. There are librarians there, so if you have trouble finding a book, you can simply ask them for help. The main reading area is filled with rows and rows of bookshelves. The books are organized by category, so it's pretty easy to find what you're looking for. There are also several computers that visitors can use to search for books. Another thing I really like about the library is its atmosphere. The whole place is very quiet and peaceful. Everyone tries to keep their voice down, so it's really easy to concentrate on what you're reading. I used to spend hours there reading all kinds of books. For me, it was the perfect place to get away from distractions and just focus on reading. So, if I wanted a quiet place to read or study, that library was always my first choice.",ko:"제가 가장 자주 가던 도서관은 Negeok Library입니다. 혼자 살던 당시 집에서 걸어서 5분 정도로 매우 가까웠고 약속이 없을 때마다 혼자 가서 몇 시간씩 책을 읽곤 했습니다. 외관에 대한 구체적인 사실은 제공되지 않아 답변에는 선택 가능한 표현을 괄호로 남겨두었습니다. 입구 근처에는 안내 데스크와 사서들이 있고, 안쪽에는 책으로 가득 찬 책장이 줄지어 있습니다. 책은 분류별로 정리되어 있고 검색용 컴퓨터도 있습니다. 전체적으로 매우 조용하고 평화로워 독서에 집중하기 좋은 곳이었습니다."}
